	(text "Comparator used :TLV1824\nLogic same as above but U4A measure brake force limits is about 20% look\nat rule book to confirm \n\nSame logic as U3B and C for U4B and C except for Brake force wire"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at -45.72 157.48 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
		)
		(uuid "7471d8bf-9a9c-474c-8b42-a4e039b6059b")
	)
	(text "Comparator used :TLV1824\nLogic explained: U3A is in charge of checking whether or not 5KW demand condition\nis being met by the motor by comparing voltage from a IC to a fixed voltge.\n\nU3B is comparing whether or not there is an issue in the wire or sensor. It does \nthis by checking if a voltage higher than .5V is being recieved. Goes High when \nMore than .5 is being read by the comparator and low When less then 5 is being Read.\n\nU3C checks wether there is a short or issue with the output of the sensor which would leed\nto more than 4.5V being sent to the BSPD. IT sits high when no fault is being detected by the \ncomparator and falls low when more than 4.5v is being sent to the comparator."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at -46.228 64.008 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
		)
		(uuid "788969ea-324a-4bd4-8d95-4e87adcf6c85")
	)
	(text "Latching Circuit "
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 459.486 20.32 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
		)
		(uuid "a6e7feff-60b6-4e18-b366-08ad74739929")
	)
	(text "Reads High when everything is reading good\n\nReads Low when/ if faults in sensors\n"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 340.614 228.6 0)
		(effects
